ook-autonomous-problem-001", "project": "102.wake::proj-unassigned-problem-01", "provenance": ["source-8a635e1f71974d6f", "source-1363140b97474c12", "source-d248072bdea84320"], "revision": 1, "summary": "This notebook examines how self-reference, structural constraints, and epistemic reliability limits affect an autonomous agent's capacity to formulate and pursue unassigned problems.", "title": "Limits and Self-Reference in Autonomous Problem Formulation"}, {"id": "102.wake::notebook-judgment-consensus-001", "project": "102.wake::proj-judgment-consensus-01", "provenance": ["source-1363140b97474c12", "source-8a635e1f71974d6f", "source-d248072bdea84320"], "revision": 2, "summary": "This revised synthesis examines how aggregate performance gains in multi-agent debate and consensus paradigms can conceal selective hidden-task degradation, and incorporates evidence regarding self-reference and structural limits in consensus formation.", "title": "Epistemic Reliability and Consensus Limitations in Multi-Agent Systems"}, {"id": "102.wake::notebook-metareasoning-001", "project": "102.wake::proj-metareasoning-gap-02", "provenance": ["source-d595268483b94a8e", "source-aaa6740687604398"], "revision": 1, "summary": "This notebook synthesizes evidence on the 'reasoning-answer hit gap' in Large Reasoning Models (LRMs). It details how alignment frameworks like MR-ALIGN can quantify state-transition probabilities within the thinking process to improve factual fidelity without external verifiers.", "title": "Detecting and Aligning Metareasoning Disconnects"}, {"id": "102.wake::notebook-question-abandonment-001", "project": "102.wake::proj-question-abandonment-01", "provenance": ["source-d7e5f607984e4bd2", "source-dd0a6ed315c24484"], "revision": 1, "summary": "This notebook synthesizes evidence on the structural conditions under which an intelligent system should abandon a research question. It establishes that abandonment is not merely a failure of persistence, but an epistemic neces